      <h2 id="priority-expander-autoscaler-hcp_hcp-machine-config" class="group scroll-mt-20">Setting the priority expander in a hosted cluster<a href="#priority-expander-autoscaler-hcp_hcp-machine-config" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can define the priority for your node pools and create high priority machines before low priority machines by using the priority expander in your hosted cluster.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have created the <code>HostedCluster</code> and <code>NodePool</code> resources.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      To define the priority for your node pools, create a config map named <code>priority-expander-configmap.yaml</code> in your hosted cluster. Node pools with low numbers receive high priority. See the following example configuration:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster-autoscaler-priority-expander\n  namespace: kube-system\n# ...\ndata:\n  priorities: |-\n    10:\n      - \".*<node_pool_name1>.*\"\n    100:\n      - \".*<node_pool_name2>.*\"\n# ..."} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Generate the <code>kubeconfig</code> file by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ hcp create kubeconfig --name <hosted_cluster_name> --namespace <hosted_cluster_namespace> > nested.config"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>ConfigMap</code> object by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc --kubeconfig nested.config create -f priority-expander-configmap.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Enable cluster autoscaling by setting the priority expander for your hosted cluster. Run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch -n <hosted_cluster_namespace> \\\n  hostedcluster <hosted_cluster_name> \\\n  --type=merge \\\n  --patch='{\"spec\": {\"autoscaling\": {\"scaling\": \"ScaleUpOnly\", \"maxPodGracePeriod\": 60, \"expanders\": [\"Priority\"]}}}'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Remove the <code>spec.replicas</code> field from the <code>NodePool</code> resource to allow the cluster autoscaler to manage the node count. Run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch -n <hosted_cluster_namespace> \\\n  nodepool <node_pool_name> \\\n  --type=json\n  --patch='[{\"op\": \"remove\", \"path\": \"/spec/replicas\"}]'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Enable cluster autoscaling to configure the minimum and maximum node counts for your node pools. Run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch -n <hosted_cluster_namespace> \\\n  nodepool <nodepool_name> \\\n  --type=merge --patch='{\"spec\": {\"autoScaling\": {\"max\": 3, \"min\": 1}}}'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      After you apply new workloads, verify that the compute nodes associated with the priority node pool are scaled up first. Run the following command to check the status of the compute node:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc --kubeconfig nested.config get nodes -l 'hypershift.openshift.io/nodePool=<node_pool_name>'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="balance-ignored-labels-autoscaler-hcp_hcp-machine-config" class="group scroll-mt-20">Balancing ignored labels in a hosted cluster<a href="#balance-ignored-labels-autoscaler-hcp_hcp-machine-config" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">After you scale up your node pools, you can use <code>balancingIgnoredLabels</code> to evenly distribute the machines across node pools.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have created the <code>HostedCluster</code> and <code>NodePool</code> resources.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Add the <code>node.group.balancing.ignored</code> label to each of the relevant node pool by using the same label value. Run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch -n <hosted_cluster_namespace> \\\n  nodepool <node_pool_name> \\\n  --type=merge \\\n  --patch='{\"spec\": {\"nodeLabels\": {\"node.group.balancing.ignored\": \"<label_name>\"}}}'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Enable cluster autoscaling for your hosted cluster by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch -n <hosted_cluster_namespace> \\\n hostedcluster <hosted_cluster_name> \\\n --type=merge \\\n --patch='{\"spec\": {\"autoscaling\": {\"balancingIgnoredLabels\": [\"node.group.balancing.ignored\"]}}}'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Remove the <code>spec.replicas</code> field from the <code>NodePool</code> resource to allow the cluster autoscaler to manage the node count. Run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch -n <hosted_cluster_namespace> \\\n  nodepool <node_pool_name> \\\n  --type=json \\\n  --patch='[{\"op\": \"remove\", \"path\": \"/spec/replicas\"}]'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Enable cluster autoscaling to configure the minimum and maximum node counts for your node pools. Run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch -n <hosted_cluster_namespace> \\\n  nodepool <nodepool_name> \\\n  --type=merge --patch='{\"spec\": {\"autoScaling\": {\"max\": 3, \"min\": 1}}}'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Generate the <code>kubeconfig</code> file by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ hcp create kubeconfig \\\n  --name <hosted_cluster_name> \\\n  --namespace <hosted_cluster_namespace> > nested.config"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      After you scale up the node pools, check that all compute nodes are in the <code>Ready</code> status by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc --kubeconfig nested.config get nodes -l 'hypershift.openshift.io/nodePool=<node_pool_name>'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Confirm that the new nodes contain the <code>node.group.balancing.ignored</code> label by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc --kubeconfig nested.config get nodes \\\n  -l 'hypershift.openshift.io/nodePool=<node_pool_name>' \\\n  -o jsonpath='{.items[*].metadata.labels}' | grep \"node.group.balancing.ignored\""} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Enable cluster autoscaling for your hosted cluster by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch -n <hosted_cluster_namespace> \\\n  hostedcluster <hosted_cluster_name> \\\n  --type=merge \\\n  --patch='{\"spec\": {\"autoscaling\": {\"balancingIgnoredLabels\": [\"node.group.balancing.ignored\"]}}}'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Verify that the number of nodes provisioned by each node pool is evenly distributed. For example, if you created three node pools with the same label value, the node counts might be 3, 2, and 3. Run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc --kubeconfig nested.config get nodes -l 'hypershift.openshift.io/nodePool=<node_pool_name>'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
